            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0368" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.6176/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stewart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-03T22:00:00-06:00">August 3, 1943—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 4—12:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>452. Reference my telegram No. 442, of July 31, 6 p.m. I have just received a
                    telegram from Reynolds who was delayed in reaching San Carlos. He informs me
                    that López is discontinuing his activities between Patuca and Coco Rivers. Thus
                    the problem appears to be solved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
